            {
              "@type": "WorkflowGroup",
              "name": "Note: Configuration",
              "description": "Wizard-editable defaults. `fetch_last_minutes` is the backfill window\nused while the watermark is missing or '0'. The macro name is scoped to\nthis playbook's UUID, so two ingestion configurations never share a\nwatermark. `max_events` fails a run whose window exceeds it -- the\nwindow fetch is count-verified and never paged, so a partial read\nmust never advance the watermark.\n",
              "type": "note",
              "isCollapsed": false,
              "hasTriggerStep": false,
              "hideInLogs": true,
              "metadata": [],
              "reusable": false,
              "top": "250",
              "left": "540",
              "height": "292",
              "width": "440",
              "uuid": "d63724fb-4ff1-572c-8589-ff8b9e200790",
              "recordTags": []
            },
            {
              "@type": "WorkflowGroup",
              "name": "Note: Environment Setup",
              "description": "Runs when the watermark macro does not exist yet, not only on the\nwizard's `vars.request.env_setup` first pass. It must come AFTER Get\nMacro Value so its absence can be seen: Update Last Pull Time only\nupdates the macro, it does not create it, so a missing macro would\notherwise leave the watermark unwritten and every run would read the\nbackfill window again without any error.\nThe macro is primed to '0', which Set Time Configuration reads as a\ncold start.\n",
              "type": "note",
              "isCollapsed": false,
              "hasTriggerStep": false,
              "hideInLogs": true,
              "metadata": [],
              "reusable": false,
              "top": "562",
              "left": "540",
              "height": "358",
              "width": "440",
              "uuid": "6611369d-51db-5961-9da4-be6fc76e3d1e",
              "recordTags": []
            },
            {
              "@type": "WorkflowGroup",
              "name": "Note: Set Time Configuration",
              "description": "`curr_timestamp` is the end of this run's window, 60 seconds behind the\nclock (see the block comment above) and in the management API's native\n`YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` (UTC) format. It is written back to the macro only\nafter Ingest succeeds, so a failed run reads its window again.\n`last_pull_time` is empty on a cold start (macro missing, or '0'); the\nrun then computes `window_from` as now minus `fetch_last_minutes`.\n",
              "type": "note",
              "isCollapsed": false,
              "hasTriggerStep": false,
              "hideInLogs": true,
              "metadata": [],
              "reusable": false,
              "top": "940",
              "left": "540",
              "height": "314",
              "width": "440",
              "uuid": "faf5bd66-c37a-57a1-a20d-b4e19b92c7a1",
              "recordTags": []
