              "recordTags": []
            },
            {
              "@type": "WorkflowGroup",
              "name": "Note: Create Record",
              "description": "The step is named \"Create Record\" because the Data Ingestion Wizard's\nData Mapping page is shown only for a create playbook with a step of\nexactly that name, and it reads the target module off this step.\n\n`is_upsert` routes this at /api/3/upsert/alerts, keyed on sourceId (the\neventId). That is the dedup that makes the Last Seen window safe: a\nwindow that is read twice, or an event re-triggered and fetched again,\nupdates its existing alert instead of duplicating it. Without it the\nplain insert path 409s on the sourceId uniqueness constraint.\n\nThe connector already clamps severity and alert_type to picklist\nmembers, so the picklist filters cannot fail with an unmapped value.\nThe date is the event's firstSeen epoch (alertDetectionDate), while\nsourcedata keeps the whole mapped payload including last_observed_epoch\nand the raw event.\n\n`description` is passed WITHOUT the `| e` escape filter: the connector\nbuilds it as sanitised rich text (inline styles only), and escaping it\nhere would store visible `<table>` markup instead of rendering the\ncard. This matches the FortiSIEM v2 ingestion playbook.\n",
              "type": "note",
              "isCollapsed": false,
              "hasTriggerStep": false,
              "hideInLogs": true,
              "metadata": [],
              "reusable": false,
              "top": "986",
              "left": "880",
              "height": "360",
              "width": "440",
              "uuid": "7d734e3d-dd41-521e-9a2e-e0329a459759",
              "recordTags": []
            },
            {
              "@type": "WorkflowGroup",
              "name": "Note: Update Last Pull Time",
              "description": "Advances the watermark only after the alerts are written, so a failed\nCreate Record leaves the window to be read again.\n",
              "type": "note",
              "isCollapsed": false,
              "hasTriggerStep": false,
              "hideInLogs": true,
